   "used": "3-5 % of the fuel energy to the piston (quiescent chambers); typical crown-centre temperature 270-310 degC for port-injected gasoline engines and 200-280 degC top ring groove with cooling gallery (1990s engines); 1.0 MW/m2 of power per piston area ~ 10 kW/L for bore/stroke ~ 1"
  },
  {
   "id": "SAE930217",
   "ref": "SAE 930217, 'Combustion Chamber Temperature and Instantaneous Local Heat Flux Measurements in a Spark Ignition Engine' (1993)",
