   "used": "peak surface heat flux 1.2-5.0 MW/m2 at wide-open throttle (2.2 L SI engine)"
  },
  {
   "id": "MIT",
   "ref": "MIT 2.61 Internal Combustion Engines, lecture 18 'Engine heat transfer'",
   "url": "https://web.mit.edu/2.61/www/Lecture%20notes/Lec.%2018%20Heat%20transf.pdf",
   "used": "SI engine peak heat flux of order 1-3 MW/m2"
  },
  {
   "id": "REV",
   "ref": "Review: 'Thermal modelling of modern engines: a review of empirical correlations to estimate the in-cylinder heat transfer coefficient'",
   "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/238186418",
   "used": "Woschni-type correlations need a calibration multiplier per engine / operating point"
  }
 ],
 "method": "rated point re-solved per Woschni multiplier with the baseline turbine area; piston heat = cycle-model piston wall heat / 16; piston FE thermal-only with that heat (gas-side Robin condition calibrated to it at the cycle wall temperature, oil-side coefficients unchanged); 'consistent' iterates the cycle piston wall temperature to the FE crown mean; hot-fatigue factor = sigma_f(T) / sigma_a at the governing elements of piston_section_fatigue.json, same data and scaling (sigma_a from the gas case, temperature-independent)"
}